  legalNotice: "Legal notice",
  privacyShort: "Privacy",
  termsShort: "Terms",
  lastUpdated: "Updated:",
  // — FAQ —
  faqSecWallet: "Wallet",
  faqSecDapps: "dApps",
  faqQ1: "How do I create a wallet?",
  faqA1:
    "On the welcome screen, tap “Create a wallet”. Kalyx generates a 12-word recovery phrase that you must write down on paper, then you verify a few words and choose a PIN code. Your keys are created directly on your phone.",
  faqQ2: "How do I restore a wallet?",
  faqA2:
    "On the welcome screen, tap “I already have a phrase”, paste your BIP-39 recovery phrase (12 or 24 words) and choose a PIN. Your wallet and its accounts are re-derived locally.",
  faqQ3: "Where is my secret phrase stored?",
  faqA3:
    "Only on your phone, encrypted with AES-256-GCM under your PIN, in the hardware secure storage (Keystore/Keychain). It is NEVER sent over the network or stored on a server.",
  faqQ4: "Can I change my PIN?",
  faqA4:
    "Yes: Settings → Change PIN. The change re-encrypts all your vaults with the new code.",
  faqQ5: "What if I lose my phone?",
  faqA5:
    "Your funds are on the blockchain, not in the phone. Install Kalyx on a new device and restore with your recovery phrase. Without that phrase, no one (including you) can access the funds — hence the importance of keeping it safe.",
  faqQ6: "Can Kalyx see my seed phrase?",
  faqA6:
    "No. Kalyx is non-custodial: your phrase is encrypted on your device, decrypted on the fly only to sign, then forgotten. It never passes through our servers.",
  faqQ7: "Why do I have to sign some transactions?",
  faqA7:
    "Any action that moves funds or authorizes a contract to spend them must be signed by your private key, protected by your PIN. This is what prevents a site from doing anything without your explicit consent.",
  faqQ8: "How do I recognize a scam?",
  faqA8: "No legitimate party will ever ask for your recovery phrase. Beware of sites imitating a known brand (Kalyx warns you in red), “unlimited” approvals and offers too good to be true. Kalyx checks sites and tokens with GoPlus, hides spam tokens and NFTs, and warns you about look-alike addresses.",
  faqQ9: "Why is my transaction pending?",
  faqA9:
    "It is waiting to be included in a block. Network fees that are too low or heavy congestion slow it down. Kalyx notifies you as soon as it is confirmed.",
  faqQ10: "How do I cancel a transaction?",
  faqA10:
    "A confirmed transaction is irreversible. A pending one can often still be replaced: on EVM networks, Speed up and Cancel are on the transaction tracking screen (same nonce, higher fee); on Bitcoin, Speed up appears in Activity, because Kalyx marks its transactions as replaceable (BIP-125). On Solana a transaction that does not land simply expires, and nothing is deducted.",
  faqQ11: "What are network fees?",
  faqA11:
    "It’s the cost paid to the network validators to process your transaction, settled in the native crypto (ETH, BNB, POL…). It varies with network congestion.",
  faqQ12: "Why did my transaction fail?",
  faqA12:
    "Common causes: insufficient balance (including fees), slippage exceeded on a swap, gas limit too low, or the contract rejected the operation. Note: the gas fees of a failed transaction are still charged.",
  faqQ13: "How do I connect a dApp?",
  faqA13: "Three ways: the Explore tab (built-in browser), WalletConnect (scan or paste a “wc:…” link) or TON Connect for TON apps (scan their QR code). In every case you confirm the connection with your PIN.",
  faqQ14: "How do I disconnect a dApp?",
  faqA14: "Menu → WalletConnect: “Disconnect” ends a WalletConnect or TON Connect session, “Forget” removes a built-in browser site. A dApp open in the Explore tab can also be disconnected from its ⋯ menu.",
  faqQ15: "What is WalletConnect?",
  faqA15:
    "A standard protocol that links your wallet to a dApp via a QR code or a link, without a browser extension.",
  faqQ16: "How do I revoke an approval?",
  faqA16:
    "Menu → Approvals: Kalyx lists the contracts you have allowed to spend your tokens. Revoke those you no longer use (it’s a transaction, with network fees).",
  faqQ17: "How do I switch networks?",
  faqA17:
    "From the home screen (the network badge) or Settings → Network. The same address works on all EVM networks; only the queried network changes.",
  faqQ18: "How do I add an RPC network?",
  faqA18:
    "Enable Expert mode, then Menu → Developer → Custom networks: enter the name, Chain ID, symbol and the RPC URL (https).",
